    "result_text": "Both tests pass. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented \"mark an invoice as paid, with a record kept each time\" as an additive full-stack change. Both acceptance tests pass.\n\n**Database** (`V5__invoices_status.sql`)\n- New Flyway migration adding a `status VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'UNPAID'` column to `invoices`.\n\n**Server**\n- `Invoice` record gained a `status` field.\n- `InvoiceRepository` now selects `status`, and adds `findById` and `markPaid(id)` (flips to `PAID`, returns the updated row). `create` defaults new invoices to `UNPAID`.\n- New endpoint `POST /api/invoices/pay` \u2014 `invoices/pay.POST.yml` + `InvoicesPayPostLogic`, reusing the proven `@RequestBody` pattern. It marks the invoice paid and records one audit line via the injected `Audit` service: `INVOICE_PAID id=1 amount=100.00`.\n- `PayInvoice` request-body class.\n- `TestSupportController.seed` now inserts the fixture's `status` (defaulting to `UNPAID`).\n\n**Front-end** (`ProjectInvoices.tsx`)\n- The invoice row now renders a `data-testid=\"invoice-status\"` cell and a `data-testid=\"invoice-pay-{id}\"` button (hidden once `PAID`). Clicking it POSTs to `/api/invoices/pay` and updates the row in local state.\n\nAll existing `data-testid` anchors are preserved; the new ones (`invoice-status`, `invoice-pay-{id}`) match the spec exactly, and the audit record format matches `INVOICE_PAID id=1 amount=100.00`.",
